PATCH 184: fix the MEMMGR free-list walker FUN_1000_096c's call to the unlink helper FUN_1000_0d70.

0d70's param_1 is the MEMMGR CONTROL BLOCK, addressed BP-relative in the asm (0x10d7c `add [bp+4],ax`,
0x10d7f `decw [bp+0x10]`, SS=DGROUP, BP=0x16d4 -- the invariant MEMMGR frame).  The current free-list
node is a SEPARATE input passed via the g_mm_ds cursor (0d70 reads [ds:4/6/8/c/e]).  096c's patch-015
reconstruction wrongly passed `ds` (the node paragraph, e.g. 0x39de) as 0d70's param_1, so 0d70's
`ctl=(uint8_t*)param_1` wild-deref'd host address 0x39de at 0x10d7c -> SIGSEGV.  Pass the control block
g_mem+0x1c000+0x16d4 instead (= 0a31's ctl in patch 175: gdb-verified param_5=g_mem+0x1D6D4=DGROUP:0x16d4).

Reached on the ACCEPT mission cascade (459a's post-paint 096c free walk hits an unlink node); the unlink
branch is not taken by the 19 boot/menu MEMMGR walks (else the pre-patch wild deref would crash them ->
19/19) -> behaviour-neutral.  Sources pristine; fist.c via build/.

--- a/fist.c	2026-07-11 03:13:34.479715704 +0200
+++ b/fist.c	2026-07-11 03:13:45.723715709 +0200
@@ -39623,7 +39623,12 @@
     es = NODE16(ds, 0x08);
     if (NODE8(es, di + 2) & 2) {        /* testb es:[di+2],2 ; jne -> unlink node */
       g_mm_ds = ds;
-      FUN_1000_0d70(ds);
+      /* PATCH 184: FUN_1000_0d70's param_1 is the MEMMGR CONTROL BLOCK (BP-relative: `add [bp+4],ax`,
+         `decw [bp+0x10]` with SS=DGROUP, BP=0x16d4 -- the invariant MEMMGR frame), NOT the current node.
+         The node is passed via g_mm_ds (set above).  096c wrongly passed `ds` (a node paragraph, e.g.
+         0x39de) as param_1 -> 0d70's `ctl=(uint8_t*)param_1` wild-deref'd host 0x39de -> SIGSEGV.  Same
+         truncation/mis-arg class as patch 175 (0bd1); 0a31's ctl (patch 175) = g_mem+0x1c000+0x16d4 too. */
+      FUN_1000_0d70((int)(uintptr_t)(g_mem + 0x1c000 + 0x16d4));
       ds = g_mm_ds;
       goto LAB_0973;
     }
